## Lore

Metallic, insect-like monsters covered in long slashing blades, not unlike a
Xiticix warrior but far more brutal. Their origin is lost; they once served the
same supernatural master as the soul worms and became the worms'' bodyguards and
servants after that master fell. Inix of Cibola has recruited thousands of them,
more than any other being, and they are the core of the city''s defenders.

Pincer warriors revel in slaughter, fear nothing and respect only strength.
They grow larger with every level of experience, and some scholars of the
supernatural believe they feed on the life force of what they kill. They prefer
their own blades but will use energy rifles, heavy weapons or flying platforms
when it suits them.

## GM Notes

Most pincer warriors are near-mindless creatures of instinct that see every
other sapient race as prey; only soul worms, gods and other supernatural beings
can cow them. A player character is an aberration and should be played as one -
hunted by its own kind, and treated as a dangerous monster nearly everywhere
else.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'cibola-pincer-warrior');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
